  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Slope of normal to $y=f(x)$ at (3,4) is $\\frac{-1}{f^{\\prime}(3)}$.\r\n$\\text { Thus, } \\begin{array}{c}\r\n\\frac{-1}{\\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(3)}=\\tan \\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right)=\\tan \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\\r\n=-\\cot \\frac{\\pi}{4}=-1 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(3)=1\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
